The repository maintains three custom-card types: the lighting card, theme settings and action links. The legacy lighting name is an alias of the same component. Shell, Energy and the three household-card presentation adapters are separately listed in the [compatibility register](../home-assistant/compatibility-register.html); an adapter is not another installed card. The [Home Assistant specifications](../home-assistant/index.html) provide design and acceptance guidance. The [interface census](../home-assistant/interface-coverage.html) now maps each entry in the pinned built-in registries, including shared controls, settings and tools; it is more specific than the original 30-gap task list.

The [terminology supplement](../content/home-assistant-terminology.html) records the official glossary, entity domains and selected native vocabulary. Use its explicit source denominators and version boundaries. It does not claim every vendor-defined integration label or future custom card has been reviewed.

## Adaptation decisions

NHS identity rules, clinical urgency and NHS-number collection are not copied into a household application. We use civica artwork, describe household consequences directly and adapt the identifier pattern to useful device and configuration identifiers. The [BSL pattern](../patterns/british-sign-language.html) makes signed-content availability, production and review requirements explicit; it does not invent a verified household video.

Publishing ministerial, organisation, statistical and policy templates become household owners, guides, reports and collections. They retain useful editorial structure while omitting government authority claims. Some patterns describe a future authored application; do not infer that a native dashboard now includes a publishing backend.

