## Brand, writing and whole-system review

The [brand inventory](../reference/brand-guidance.json) and [writing inventory](../reference/writing-guide.json) add source-to-rule mappings for the new guidance. They record relevant chapters, deliberate adaptations and excluded material rather than treating a source homepage link as full coverage.

The [work-package checklist](guidance-work-package.html) records repeated coverage checks. The [whole-system audit](design-system-audit.html) records the review scope, every-page outcomes and confirmed findings. The [component organisation review](component-audit.html) and [missing-specification register](missing-components.html) record implemented shared ownership and the 30 dedicated native-task design specifications. None of these records changes a reference example into an installed Home Assistant feature.

## Maintain coverage

When an upstream index changes, compare entries recursively, record the reviewed version or date and update the mapping. Read a component’s actual source before changing its local behaviour. Keep source status, local examples and native implementation status separate. The documentation checks reject missing mapped pages and broken local routes.

When a source component is withdrawn, preserve the stable local URL, explain the reason and link to the replacement. Do not silently delete guidance that existing dashboards or issue reports may reference.
